// Title: WMI Persistence - Command Line Event Consumer
// Sigma ID: 05936ce2-ee05-4dae-9d03-9a391cf2d2c6
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Thomas Patzke
// Date: 2018-03-07 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1546.003, persistence
// Description: Detects WMI command line event consumers
// False positives:
//   - Unknown (data set is too small; further testing needed)
// References:
//   - https://www.eideon.com/2018-03-02-THL03-WMIBackdoors/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_wmi_persistence_commandline_event_consumer.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\wbem\\WmiPrvSE.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\wbemcons.dll"
